	(text "External +5 V (J17, priority)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 41.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "afc51bc0-ab63-5de9-a46c-9929726f9288")
	)
	(text "J11 keeps the original CPU board connector (IO board J16 harness) for +5 V and ground only: its +-12 V pins are not used.\nThe audio amplifiers run from an external +12 V supply on J23 (about 3 A at full volume). F1 + D5 blow the fuse on reverse polarity.\nU3 NCP1117 (as in the RP2350 hardware guide) is stable with ceramic capacitors. All regulator capacitors are 0805 or larger for low DC-bias derating.\nExternal +5 V on J17 has priority: U2 turns the J11 path off whenever +5V_EXT is present (EXT_PRESENT high).\nLTC4412 + AO3401A ideal diodes stand in for the TPS2121 of ARCHITECTURE.md 9.3 (library part, about 4 A per path).\nJP1 (bridged by default) disconnects the J11 +5 V completely; leaving J17 unplugged forces J11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bde62702-015c-5283-acf0-2bdd4e0c270f")
	)
	(text "IO board power (J11, +5 V only)"
